equire its in-process-read statement; mirror_guard's module docstring is excluded because argparse publishes it.\n\nConcise/load-bearing source prose outside the allowlist stays byte-identical. So do runtime strings, assertions, fixtures, decorators, subprocess arguments, config values, and all directive/shebang physical lines. The only non-Python change is generated docs/env-vars.md: 5 config.py source-line references shifted by this comment shortening; environment keys and behavior remain unchanged.\n\n## Verification and independent review\nParse base and final Python with `type_comments=True`; replace only allowlisted leading owner docstrings, normalize only `ast.TypeIgnore.lineno`, and require the remaining AST/runtime tree to match. A zero-context base-to-final hunk guard and independent block receipts restrict every change to the surviving allowlist at 7840899ea7ac0609bf3e0dec5e26effdbda1ec6c. Run all six structured DD commands, including exact one-commit paths, focused consumers, scoped diff integrity, hygiene, and untimed worktree-venv `make verify`.\n\nA reviewer who did not author the patch records a leaf-linked TSV with exactly 120 PASS rows, one per stable ID: `stable_id,before_citation,final_citation,preserved_contract_or_consumer,directives_exact,before_words,final_words,reviewer_session,semantic_pass,bloat_pass`. Every `final_words` is smaller; missing, extra, duplicate, or FAIL rows block closure.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Exactly 120 allowlisted blocks have smaller final word counts.\n- [x] Non-allowlisted prose and all directive/shebang lines remain exact.\n- [x] The immutable-base runtime/non-comment oracle passes for every owned file.\n- [x] Every preserved contract or consumer has an independent TSV PASS citation.\n- [x] HEAD^..HEAD changes exactly the 12 source paths plus generated docs/env-vars.md and focused, diff-integrity, and hygiene checks exit 0.\n- [x] Untimed worktree-venv `make verify` exits 0."}},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-